B.G3=new A.h9("Spellbound","This project was created for UGAHacks 11, and aimed to gamify the study experience by rewarding users for remaining in designated work zones like the Zell Miller Learning Center or Main Library. My primary contribution was the implementation of the geofencing feature using packages and APIs like OpenStreetMaps and LatLng2 in Flutter. I engineered a system that creates a real-time stream of the user\u2019s coordinates to verify their physical presence at a location, which is continually updated to make sure that users stay within their study location to verify that they are in a \u2018focus session\u2019. This is done with a distance function that the app uses to determine the distance between the user and the nearest study spot. If the user moves outside a defined radius, then the app automatically pauses their session and stops their progress. This project gave me hands-on experience with asynchronous programming in Dart and handling location streams. It was a great challenge to balance GPS accuracy with battery efficiency during long focus sessions. I worked on Spellbound with my amazing teammates Matyas Beyene and Bornini Chandra.","https://spellboundhacks.github.io/","Summary: Developed skills in geofencing and geotagging locations, as well as using the OpenStreetMaps API and LatLng2 package to handle constant location streams to track where users are.",B.hE,null)
B.BK=s(["lib/images/efficiSS.png","lib/images/efficiSS2.png","lib/images/EfficiSS3.png"],t.ee)
B.G4=new A.h9("Effici (2023)","My first ever dive into Flutter! Particularly, I decided to build a calendar and productivity based app that could help people organize their lives more easily. This idea culminated in the form of Effici, which is not just a calendar app but a easy-to-use personal time-management interface. It differentiates itself from other similar calendar apps by adding functionality that allows the user to take notes within each event. This allows for easy recall and location of notes when users need to find information about specific events on specific days. With simple yet stunning Material Design elements and an intuitive event creation system that allows for even the newest users to quickly become proficient in using it, Effici works to ultimately redefine how you organize your life. With it, I aimed to say goodbye to cluttered schedules for all and hello to seamless planning. With this project, I also established my baseline knowledge of Flutter and learned how to use basic widgets, design simple but effective UI, and also employ SQFLite as my database solution to persist data across app restarts.","","Summary: My first ever Flutter project in which I created a productivity app that allows you to use it as both a calendar and seamless notetaker!",B.BK,null)
B.BL=s(["lib/images/weatherwispSS.png","lib/images/weatherwispSS2.png"],t.ee)
B.G5=new A.h9("Weather Wisp (2024)","A new take on my past Flutter projects, I focused more on gaining proficiency with using external APIs in the Flutter framework and improving the UX for users in a way that's easily digestible by using glassmorphic design, similar to the current approach at companies like Apple! This was initially challenging to grasp, a external APIs in Flutter can often have slight variances in the way they need to be used in order to be maximally effective. However, with time, I was able to create a simple yet sophisticated design that reflects the weather conditions externally. Overall, I greatly improved the user experience skills I wanted to hone. Learning to use APIs has been a very valuable and rewarding skill to learn - one that will come in very handy in the future for larger scale projects.","https://weatherwisp.github.io/","Summary: A Flutter project where I focused on honing my API skills and learnt to integrate various different APIs and packages into my projects!",B.BL,null)
B.AT=s(["lib/images/portfolioss1.png","lib/images/portfolioss2.png"],t.ee)
B.G6=new A.h9("Redesigned Portfolio","This personal portfolio website, built entirely with Flutter as usual, helped me learn and experiment with cutting-edge UI/UX design principles that not include Material design but also responsive design, which entails creating an experience that fits multiple screen sizes and content experiences, allowing me to create a product that is a more visually appealing and accessible to all types of devices than ever before. During the development of this site, I once again used AGILE strategies and used them to hone my skills at self-regulation and organization that I believe will be highly useful in my future endeavors. Overall, this was a highly enriching experience that taught me the value of leveraging Flutter's rich widget library and extensive developer package community to be able to develop a dynamic website that seamlessly adapts to various screen sizes by prioritizing intuitive navigation and user engagement.","https://nandanpraveen.github.io/","Summary: Learned new methods of UI, UX, and color design that were used to develop the current site you are on!",B.AT,null)
B.C0=s(["lib/images/flappySS.png","lib/images/flappyGIF.gif"],t.ee)
B.G7=new A.h9("Flappy Bird AI (2024)","For this project, I strayed away from my typical Flutter roots and began experimenting with Python and the NEAT framework to build an AI that could play Flappy Bird with team members at Innovation Academy. We began with tutorials and reading online articles, but after grasping the concepts through following one such tutorial, it became easier to conceptually understand what was happening behind-the-scenes in the neural network. It was an extremely rewarding experience to eventually see the AI become a master at playing Flappy Bird. I worked on the reward function and optimizing the reward for desirable actions while penalizing negative ones, and to see generations became progressively better before bursting into exponential skill growth truly made me appreciate the formidable artificial intelligence player we have made. I'm excited to use the knowledge I've gained in this project for applications in my future projects both in and outside the domain of Flutter, for things like AI chatbots in applications and medical uses of AI to detect health issues through images.","","Summary: A Pygame and NEAT focused project where I experimented with using AI and reinforcement learning to teach a computer how to play Flappy Bird!",B.C0,null)
B.BM=s(["lib/images/cureconnectSS.png","lib/images/cureconnectSS2.png"],t.ee)
B.G8=new A.h9("CureConnect (2024)","For this project, I went back to my Flutter roots and began experimenting with making solutions for people in underprivileged communities that can give them access to easily achievable and affordable medical solutions. With CureConnect, I aim to help people bring the power of medicine to the fingertips of all. By clicking just a few filters that specify the ingredients they have access to, CureConnect uses a sorting algorithm I developed to present all the different home remedies a user can make. It does this while rightfully attributing the correct sources and also acting as an offline resource. This is to acknowledge the fact that it can make it more affordable and accessible for people who may not have constant internet access. CureConnect will be updated regularly with new cures and information to further increase the scope of usage for users in underprivileged communities globally. I am looking forward to having this published on the Play Store, and am glad I got the chance to learn about sorting algorithms and hone my UI skills.","","Summary: A return to Flutter-based projects where I created an offline system for impoverished communities to note their home remedies and find new ones!",B.BM,null)
B.Co=s(["lib/images/outreachSS.png","lib/images/outreachSS2.png"],t.ee)
B.G9=new A.h9("IA Outreach Web App (2024)","My second run with Flutter, where I learnt proficiency with Firebase, data management, and improving the UX for end users to make it easy for anyone to understand. Learning Firebase was particularly difficult at first, as I didn't know if I should focus on Firestore or Authentication first. However, as I gradually found my way through using Firestore to first implement basic systems like making events that were visible to all users, I progressed to creating more complex systems like login. With this app, I became proficient in creating authentication systems and managing and linking data between the login and load time of the app. Overall, it was an enriching experience that has improved my proficiency with Flutter exponentially. Fun fact, this system is currently being used at the FCS Innovation Academy for 150+ students year round!","https://iaoutreach.github.io/","Summary: My second Flutter project where I made an internal events management system and learnt to use Firebase Firestore and Authentication!",B.Co,null)
B.Cu=s(["lib/images/mathgame.png","lib/images/mathgamegif.gif"],t.ee)
B.Ga=new A.h9("Fraction Dash (2025)","Fraction Dash represents my first ever attempt at building a video game with my knowledge of Flutter, and also learning to use animations in the framework! I set out with a small team of 4 to build an educational game that helped 5th graders learn the Georgia math standard of fraction addition, and we brainstormed the idea of a racing game! In Fraction Dash, users can race on three different difficulties of tracks where they need to solve fraction addition problems to earn RacerPoints, an in-game currency that allows them to buy powerups that boost their speed, freeze time, and even reset their time! The goal of the game is to ultimately reach the finish line as quickly as possible. YouTube tutorials were particularly useful in learning the skills needed to interpolate the animations of the car moving around the track. This project made me realize that animations are much easier than I had previously thought, and reinforced the idea that I can learn any Flutter skill with enough time and patience. I am most proud of my work on the powerups in the game, as they add lots of complexity to the game and make it much more interesting for young learners to play. I hope that with this game, I'm able to help young learners learn to add fractions in a way that is less tedious and brain-numbing than working through a textbook page. I would love to keep working on this project in the future and believe that if I had to restart it, I would repeat everything but work on the animations with my team earlier so that we can improve the graphical fidelity of the car, track, and general UI.","https://akarshkudrimoti.github.io/fractiondash/","Summary: My first ever Flutter game-based project where I tried to build a racing game to teach elementary school students fractions!",B.Cu,null)
